E('charles darwin|darwin|evolution|natural selection|origin of species', 'Charles Darwin was an English naturalist whose theory of evolution by natural selection transformed biology.', 'He lived from 1809 to 1882.',
  'He sailed around the world on HMS Beagle from 1831 to 1836.', 'Finches and tortoises on the Galápagos Islands helped shape his ideas.', 'He published On the Origin of Species in 1859.', 'Natural selection means individuals better suited to their environment tend to survive and have more offspring.', 'Alfred Russel Wallace reached similar ideas independently.', 'He waited about twenty years before publishing.',
  'Evolution is the unifying idea of modern biology.')
E('gregor mendel|mendel|genetics', 'Gregor Mendel was an Austrian monk known as the father of genetics.', 'He lived from 1822 to 1884.',
  'He bred about 28,000 pea plants in his monastery garden.', 'He found that traits are passed on in predictable patterns.', 'He described dominant and recessive traits.', 'His work was ignored until about 1900.',
  'His discoveries are the foundation of modern genetics.')
E('dna|double helix|watson and crick|rosalind franklin', 'DNA is the molecule that carries genetic instructions in living things.', 'Its double-helix structure was described in 1953.',
  'James Watson and Francis Crick published the model.', 'Rosalind Franklin’s X-ray image, “Photo 51”, was crucial evidence.', 'Franklin died in 1958 and was not included in the 1962 Nobel Prize.', 'DNA is made of four bases: A, T, C and G.', 'The Human Genome Project finished sequencing human DNA in 2003.',
  'It launched modern molecular biology and genetic medicine.')
E('louis pasteur|pasteur|pasteurisation|pasteurization', 'Louis Pasteur was a French chemist and microbiologist.', 'He lived from 1822 to 1895.',
  'He showed that germs cause disease and fermentation.', 'He developed pasteurisation, heating liquids to kill microbes.', 'He created vaccines for rabies and anthrax.', 'He disproved the idea that life arises spontaneously.',
  'His work saved countless lives.')
E('vaccines|edward jenner|smallpox|vaccination', 'Vaccines train the immune system to fight diseases.', 'Edward Jenner developed the first vaccine, against smallpox, in 1796.',
  'Jenner noticed milkmaids who caught cowpox seemed protected from smallpox.', 'The word vaccine comes from the Latin vacca, meaning cow.', 'A global campaign eradicated smallpox, declared in 1980.', 'It is the only human disease ever fully eradicated.',
  'Vaccines are among the greatest public health achievements in history.')
E('penicillin|alexander fleming|fleming|antibiotics', 'Penicillin was the first widely used antibiotic.', 'Alexander Fleming discovered it in 1928.',
  'He noticed mould killing bacteria on a dish left out while he was on holiday.', 'Howard Florey and Ernst Chain turned it into a usable medicine in the 1940s.', 'It saved many soldiers in the Second World War.', 'The three shared the Nobel Prize in 1945.', 'Overuse of antibiotics has led to resistant bacteria.',
  'Antibiotics transformed medicine.')
E('florence nightingale|nightingale', 'Florence Nightingale was a British nurse and statistician who founded modern nursing.', 'She lived from 1820 to 1910.',
  'She led nurses in the Crimean War in the 1850s.', 'She was called “the Lady with the Lamp” for her night rounds.', 'She improved hygiene, sharply cutting death rates.', 'She used pioneering charts to show data.',
  'International Nurses Day is held on her birthday, 12 May.')
E('nikola tesla|tesla|alternating current', 'Nikola Tesla was a Serbian-American inventor and electrical engineer.', 'He lived from 1856 to 1943.',
  'He developed the alternating current (AC) electrical system.', 'AC won the “war of the currents” against Edison’s direct current.', 'He invented the induction motor and the Tesla coil.', 'He experimented with wireless power.', 'He died poor in New York.',
  'Most of the world’s electricity runs on AC.')
E('thomas edison|edison|light bulb|lightbulb', 'Thomas Edison was an American inventor and businessman.', 'He lived from 1847 to 1931.',
  'He held 1,093 US patents.', 'He invented the phonograph in 1877.', 'He developed a practical, long-lasting light bulb in 1879.', 'He built the first electric power station in New York.', 'His research lab at Menlo Park was a model for modern labs.',
  'He helped build the electrified modern world.')
E('alexander graham bell|telephone|graham bell', 'Alexander Graham Bell was a Scottish-born inventor credited with the telephone.', 'He lived from 1847 to 1922 and patented the telephone in 1876.',
  'His first words over it were, “Mr Watson, come here, I want to see you.”', 'He also worked as a teacher of deaf people.', 'Others, like Antonio Meucci and Elisha Gray, worked on similar devices.',
  'The telephone changed communication forever.')
E('wright brothers|first flight|kitty hawk', 'The Wright brothers, Orville and Wilbur, made the first powered, controlled airplane flight.', 'It happened on 17 December 1903, at Kitty Hawk, North Carolina.',
  'The first flight lasted 12 seconds and covered 37 metres.', 'They ran a bicycle shop in Dayton, Ohio.', 'Their key breakthrough was controlling the plane in the air.',
  'Within decades, flight had transformed travel and warfare.')
E('henry ford|ford|model t|assembly line', 'Henry Ford was an American industrialist who made cars affordable.', 'He lived from 1863 to 1947.',
  'He launched the Model T in 1908.', 'His moving assembly line, from 1913, cut build time dramatically.', 'He paid workers $5 a day, high for the time.', 'He said customers could have any colour “so long as it is black”.', 'He also spread antisemitic views.',
  'Mass production transformed industry worldwide.')
E('stephen hawking|hawking', 'Stephen Hawking was an English theoretical physicist.', 'He lived from 1942 to 2018.',
  'He was diagnosed with motor neurone disease at 21.', 'He predicted that black holes give off radiation, now called Hawking radiation.', 'His book A Brief History of Time sold over 10 million copies.', 'He communicated using a speech-generating device.',
  'He made cosmology popular with millions.')
E('periodic table|mendeleev|dmitri mendeleev', 'The periodic table organises the chemical elements.', 'Dmitri Mendeleev published the first widely recognised version in 1869.',
  'He arranged elements by atomic weight and properties.', 'He left gaps for elements not yet discovered and predicted their properties.', 'Today there are 118 known elements.',
  'It is the central map of chemistry.')
E('big bang|origin of the universe', 'The Big Bang theory explains how the universe began expanding from a hot, dense state.', 'It happened about 13.8 billion years ago.',
  'Georges Lemaître, a Belgian priest and physicist, first proposed it.', 'Edwin Hubble showed galaxies are moving away from us.', 'The leftover heat, the cosmic microwave background, was found in 1965.',
  'It is the leading scientific explanation of the universe’s origin.')
E('edwin hubble|hubble|hubble telescope|hubble space telescope', 'Edwin Hubble was an American astronomer, and the Hubble Space Telescope is named after him.', 'He lived from 1889 to 1953; the telescope launched in 1990.',
  'He proved other galaxies exist beyond the Milky Way.', 'He showed the universe is expanding.', 'The telescope orbits about 540 kilometres above Earth.', 'Its mirror had a flaw fixed by astronauts in 1993.',
  'Hubble’s images transformed our view of the cosmos.')
E('quantum mechanics|quantum physics|quantum', 'Quantum mechanics is the physics of very small things, like atoms and particles.', 'It developed in the early 20th century.',
  'Max Planck proposed in 1900 that energy comes in packets called quanta.', 'Niels Bohr, Werner Heisenberg and Erwin Schrödinger were key figures.', 'Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle says you can’t know a particle’s exact position and momentum at once.', 'Schrödinger’s cat is a thought experiment about a cat both alive and dead.',
  'It underlies lasers, computer chips and MRI scanners.')
E('internet|world wide web|tim berners-lee|www', 'The internet is a global network of computers; the World Wide Web is a system of pages that runs on it.', 'ARPANET began in 1969; the Web was invented in 1989.',
  'ARPANET was funded by the US Department of Defense.', 'Vint Cerf and Bob Kahn designed TCP/IP, the internet’s core protocols.', 'Tim Berners-Lee invented the Web at CERN.', 'He made it free for everyone.',
  'It changed how billions of people live, work and communicate.')
E('alan turing|turing|enigma|codebreakers', 'Alan Turing was an English mathematician, codebreaker and a founder of computer science.', 'He lived from 1912 to 1954.',
  'He helped break the German Enigma code at Bletchley Park in the Second World War.', 'Their work may have shortened the war by years.', 'He described a theoretical “Turing machine”, the basis of computers.', 'He proposed the Turing test for machine intelligence.', 'He was prosecuted for being gay in 1952, and received a royal pardon in 2013.',
  'He is now honoured on the UK £50 note.')
E('computer|first computer|computers|ada lovelace|charles babbage', 'Computers have their roots in 19th-century machines and 20th-century electronics.', 'Charles Babbage designed his Analytical Engine in the 1830s.',
  'Ada Lovelace wrote what is seen as the first computer program for it.', 'ENIAC, finished in 1945, was an early electronic general-purpose computer.', 'The transistor was invented in 1947.', 'Microchips followed in the late 1950s.', 'Personal computers spread from the late 1970s.',
  'Computers now run almost everything in modern life.')
